    <!--
      User-facing strings.

      Until now this file held exactly one entry (app_name) and every other
      string was a literal in a composable, so the app could not show Hebrew at
      all while the web has had an EN/HE toggle for months.

      Scope matches the web on purpose: CHROME and interface text are
      translated; dashboard names, slugs and probe values stay English, because
      they are identifiers rather than prose and translating them would make the
      app and the console disagree about what a thing is called.
    -->
